+Fix $a\in A$. Here $A$ and $B$ are unary, as in the statement. After translating the input and restricting to a small punctured disc about $a$, Lemma~\ref{lim:exists}, applied with the closed bounded target $\overline B$, gives a finite minimal limit. Its cardinality is at most one by \cite[Lemma~9.4]{Yin:special:trans}. It is nonempty because the function has a value at every point of the punctured disc. Write this limit as $\{b\}$.
